#. Tag: title
#: pageformat.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting the Page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before delving into the specifics of formatting a page in &kword;, remember "
"that &kword; has two separate types of documents: Text Oriented and Page "
"Layout. Please review <link linkend=\"wp-vs-dtp\">The difference between "
"Text Oriented and Page Layout Documents</link>, if the differences are still "
"unclear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the manual is divided into two sub-parts, one for <link "
"linkend=\"wp-page-format\">Text Oriented</link>, the other for <link linkend="
"\"dtp-page-format\">Page Layout</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: pageformat.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting the Page (Text Oriented Document)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: pageformat.docbook:24 pageformat.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "text oriented document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: pageformat.docbook:24 pageformat.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting the page size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: pageformat.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting the page size (text oriented document)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: pageformat.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting the margins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: pageformat.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting the margins (text oriented document)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: pageformat.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "headers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: pageformat.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: pageformat.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "footers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: pageformat.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting the page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are working with a Text Oriented Document, you control the size and "
"shape of the main frame by setting the paper size and the margins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:34 pageformat.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Formatting the page is usually done by selecting: <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Page Layout...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also go straight to the <guimenuitem> Page Layout</guimenuitem> "
"options by selecting the main frame of the document and then double clicking "
"on either of the rulers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A dialog box will appear with three tabs, labeled <guilabel>Page Size &amp; "
"Margins</guilabel>, <guilabel>Columns</guilabel> and <guilabel>Header &amp; "
"and Footer</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:46 pageformat.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Page Size &amp; Margins</guilabel> tab is for altering the "
"paper size, and changing the margins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:56 pageformat.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First you will notice, that a preview box appears on the right half of this "
"dialog. This will <emphasis>approximate</emphasis> the final look of your "
"document. It is updated with each change, and should be used as a guide for "
"your changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:61 pageformat.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left, the dialog displays the current unit of measurement. This unit "
"of measurement is the same unit of measurement you use for your document "
"rulers. (In this example, we are using inches.) To change the units, follow "
"the instructions in the section entitled <link linkend=\"rulers\">Using "
"Rulers</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:67 pageformat.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The dialog section labeled <guilabel>Page Size</guilabel> is used to specify "
"the paper size for the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:69 pageformat.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; includes many predefined paper sizes. Select the appropriate paper "
"size with the drop down box labeled <guilabel>Size</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:72 pageformat.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to standard paper sizes, there are two selections that deserve "
"special mention."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: pageformat.docbook:76 pageformat.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen"
msgstr "Ecran"

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:77 pageformat.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This format is used to generate a document where each page has an <glossterm "
"linkend=\"defaspectratio\">aspect ratio</glossterm> (shape) which matches "
"the aspect ratios of computer monitors. This might be useful for documents "
"which will never be printed, but will appear only on a computer screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: pageformat.docbook:84 pageformat.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom"
msgstr "Personalizat"

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:85 pageformat.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can select this option to specify a unique paper size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:86 pageformat.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once selected, two text entry boxes (labeled <guilabel>Width:</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Height:</guilabel>) become active. Enter the height and width of "
"your desired paper size in these text boxes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the page size, are two radio boxes in the section labeled "
"<guilabel>Orientation</guilabel> you can select either <link linkend="
"\"defportrait\">Portrait</link> or <link linkend=\"deflandscape\">Landscape</"
"link> layout for your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the page orientation, is the <guilabel>Margins</guilabel> subsection, "
"which consists of 4 spin boxes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Margins</guilabel> define the white-space surrounding the text "
"in your main frame. You can enter any number from 0 to the maximum size of "
"the page in these boxes. The units are the same for all four boxes, and is "
"the same as the measurement listed at the top of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on the <guilabel>Columns</guilabel> tab allows you to change the "
"number of columns on each page. Details on multi-column documents can be "
"found <link linkend=\"columns\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on the <guilabel>Header &amp; Footer</guilabel> tab allows the user "
"to specify header and footer information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "This dialog can be broken into two major sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are not familiar with Headers and Footers yet, you should first read "
"the section entitled <link linkend=\"headers-and-footers\">Headers/Footers</"
"link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: pageformat.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "Headers"
msgstr "Caps"

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section lets you determine the placement of headers, and which pages "
"have which headers on them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you place a mark in front of <guilabel>Different header for the first "
"page</guilabel>, you will be able to specify a different format for the "
"header on the first page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you place a mark in front of <guilabel>Different header for even and odd "
"pages</guilabel>, the even pages will use one header, the odd pages use "
"another header."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this to ensure the page numbers are always on the outside of the "
"page, or to list the title of the document on odd pages and the chapter "
"number on the even pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the spin box labeled <guilabel>Spacing between header and body:</"
"guilabel>, you can specify how much empty space should be placed between the "
"bottom of the header, and the top of the main frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: pageformat.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Footers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section lets you determine the placement of footers, and which pages "
"have which footers on them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you place a mark in front of <guilabel>Different footer for the first "
"page</guilabel>, you will be able to specify a different format for the "
"footer on the first page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you place a mark in front of <guilabel>Different footer for even and odd "
"pages</guilabel>, the even pages will use one footer, the odd pages use "
"another footer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the spin box labeled <guilabel>Spacing between footer and body:</"
"guilabel>, you can specify how much empty space should be placed between the "
"top of the footer, and the bottom of the main frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: pageformat.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Footnote/Endnote"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The bottom spin box is labeled <guilabel>Spacing between footnote and body:</"
"guilabel>. As the label suggests, you can use this text box to specify the "
"distance between the bottom edge of the main frame, and the top edge of the "
"footnotes. For more information on footnotes, see the section entitled <link "
"linkend=\"endnotes-and-footnotes\">footnotes</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are satisfied with the changes you are ready to make, click "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>, all your changes will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: pageformat.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Formatting the Page (Page Layout Document)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: pageformat.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "page layout document"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: pageformat.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "formatting the page size (page layout document)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are working with a Page Layout Document, you control the size and "
"shape of all the frames individually."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also go straight to the <guimenuitem>Page Layout</guimenuitem> "
"options by double clicking on either of the rulers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next to the paper format, in the section labeled <guilabel>Orientation</"
"guilabel> you can select either <link linkend=\"defportrait\">Portrait</"
"link> or <link linkend=\"deflandscape\">Landscape</link> layout for your "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: pageformat.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the page format options, is the <guilabel>Margins</guilabel> "
"subsection, which consists of 4 entry boxes. All options in this subsection "
"are disabled in Page Oriented documents."
msgstr ""
